## The upstream server

`Stirling-PDF-server.jar` v3.3.0, the MIT core release asset, reused
unmodified:

* Project: <https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-PDF>
* Release: <https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-PDF/releases/tag/v3.3.0>
* Asset: `Stirling-PDF-server.jar`
* sha256: `5cb59682f93bd7d48312d36a87585ef2e8ca9ddfa64bc210dea6bd882925557c`
* Licence: MIT (the jar's own `Implementation-Version` is 3.3.0)

The jar embeds 450 third-party libraries. Their declared names, versions and
licences are published inside the jar as
`BOOT-INF/classes/static/3rdPartyLicenses.json`, and this repository carries
that file verbatim at `licences/3rdPartyLicenses.json`. Those libraries remain
under their own licences; the MIT licence above does not cover them. `sbom.cdx.json`
lists the same set as a CycloneDX 1.5 SBOM.

